  [-]add <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Add item to given list
  [-]analyse <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Perform timing analysis
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
  [-]clear: Clears the screen (Gui mode only)
  [-]echo "text": prints the text to the console
  [-]exit: Quits the shell (Standalone mode only)
  [-]help [command/option]: Displays help message for the given command/option
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]list <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Lists the given set of items
  [-]print <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display analysis information
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]remove <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Remove item from given list
  [-]set <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set path information
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]unset <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Unset item from given list
  [-]version: Displays the version information
  [-]add <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Add item to given list
      option: branch <from LABEL_REF> <to LABEL_REF>: Adds the given from/to reference to the branches list
      option: label <LABEL_REF> <label>: Adds the given label to the labels list
      option: srclabel <SRCLABEL_REF> <label>: Adds the given source label to the source labels list
      option: endpoint <ENDPOINT_REF> <label>: Adds the given endpoint to the endpoints list
  [-]analyse <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Perform timing analysis
      option: path <from ENDPOINT_REF> <to ENDPOINT_REF>: Sets a path start and end points
      option: function <name>: Sets a path to trace a given function
  [-]clear: Clears the screen (Gui mode only)
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
      option: proc <node id> <core id>: All following analysis on given node and core (default: 0,0)
      option: freq <core frequency>: Sets the core frequency (default: 400)
      option: threads <num threads>: Sets number of threads currently executing (default: 8)
      option: srcpaths <paths>: Sets the (semicolon separated) source search path
  [-]echo "text": prints the text to the console
  [-]exit: Quits the shell (Standalone mode only)
  [-]help [command/option]: Displays help message for the given command/option
      options: LABEL_REF, SRCLABEL_REF, ENDPOINT_REF, CONSTRAINT_REF
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]list <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Lists the given set of items
      option: branches: Lists the branches
      option: labels: Lists the labels
      option: srclabels: Lists the source labels
      option: endpoints: Lists the endpoints
      option: allsrclabels: Lists all the possible locations for source labels
      option: allendpoints: Lists all the possible locations for endpoints
      option: unknowns : Displays a list of the unknowns within the current analysis
      option: functions: Lists the functions in the loaded application
      option: sources: Lists the source files
      option: times: Lists the instructions which have had their times set
      option: constraint <expression>: Displays the current constraint expression
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]print <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display analysis information
      option: summary: Show routes summary
      option: asm <route id> <path/block id>: Display annotated assembly for given path id
      option: src <route id> <path/block id>: Display annotated source file(s) for given path id
      option: mix <route id> <path/block id>: Display annotated source file(s) + assembly instructions for the given path id
      option: trace <route id> <path/block id>: Display instruction trace for the given path/block
      option: completed_paths: Show timing of complete paths
      option: completed_loops: Show timing of complete paths + loops
      option: completed_blocks: Show timing of complete paths + loops + blocks
      option: completed_instructions: Show timing of complete paths + loops + blocks + instructions
      option: unresolved_paths: Show timing of unresolved path(s)
      option: unresolved_loops: Show timing of complete paths + loops
      option: unresolved_blocks: Show timing of complete paths + loops + blocks
      option: unresolved_instructions: Show timing of complete paths + loops + blocks + instructions
      option: route_info <route id>: Show detailed information for the given route
      option: path_info <route id> <path/block id>: Show detailed information for the given path/block
      option: functions <route id>: Shows which paths touch which functions
      option: sources <route id>: Shows which paths touch which sources
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]remove <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Remove item from given list
      option: branch <from LABEL_REF>: Removes the given from reference from the branches list
      option: label [label]+: Removes the given labels from the labels list (supports regular expressions)
      option: srclabel [label]+: Removes the given source labels from the source labels list (supports regular expressions)
      option: endpoint [label]+: Removes the given endpoints from the endpoints list (supports regular expressions)
      option: route <route id>: Removes the route with the given id from the current analysis
  [-]set <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set path information
      option: loop <route id> <path id> <scope> <iterations>: Sets the number of iterations for the given route/path
          scope: relative/r: Iteration number propagates to the enclosing path (Default)
          scope: absolute/a: Absolute number of iterations
      option: time <ENDPOINT_REF> <mode> <value>: Sets the time taken for the instruction at the given pc
          mode: ns:     Sets the time this instruction takes in ns
          mode: cycles: Sets the time this instruction takes in thread cycles
      option: constraint <expression>: Defines the constraint expression
      option: maxtime <route id> <mode> <value>: Sets the maximum allowed time taken for the given route
          mode: ns:     Sets the time this instruction takes in ns
          mode: cycles: Sets the time this instruction takes in thread cycles
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]unset <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Unset item from given list
      option: time <pc>: Clears the time set for the given instructions (supports regular expressions)
      option: time <route id>: Clears the the maximum allowed time for the given route
